  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.ContextPhase` has no MUST, SHOULD or MAY clause. Its only concrete obligation is that the SDK exports a public unit struct `ContextPhase`. The prose says it marks a request that can still accept context. That behavior is carried by `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#struct[ContextPhase]`, which has an {impl} reference to `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.phases`. The `context` method exists only on `impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, ContextPhase>]`. Because that behavior is delegated to the refining requirement, it needs no test here.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` carries the {test} reference. It generates rustdoc for the crate and compares the documented exports, with their kinds, against the inventory in the requirements book. It asserts that nothing is missing or unexpected. Removing `ContextPhase`, making it private, or changing it to a different kind of item would fail that test. I found no gap.",
